<p>Weight is the measurement of gravity on a mass. Mass is still important for acceleration and other calculations like for momentum or acceleration through forces.</p>
<p>I'm assuming this screws with G for the affected matter so it's less attractive to large masses<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-515810-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-515810-1')">1</a></sup> with it eventually being reversed after the flash point.</p>
<p>The addenda is great. The containment procedure probably needs a bit more as pointed out already. May also want to specifically say that direct exposure to SCP-1703 is forbidden in the actual containment procedures. That seems pretty important.</p>
<p>Next question, what counts as direct exposure? I'm certain that video observation doesn't count, but what about via a mirror (probably) or exposure via diffraction?</p>
